From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lethalbas <lethalbas@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:06:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rt(tse,tfe): don't build RT particles outside the RT particle
 pass

TSE 1_2_Palenque demo 1 under RT crashed with an access violation in
Engine.dll (RVA 0x1922d8 = RT_GetViewVectors, Windows event 1000) at the
moment the player used the chainsaw.

Cause: the TSE-only first-person chainsaw particles are rendered from the
HUD pass (Player.es RenderHUD: Particle_PrepareSystem/PrepareEntity(this)/
RenderChainsawParticles). Under GAT_RT, Particle_RenderSquare goes to
RT_Particle_RenderSquare, and RT_GetViewVectors checked only
_Particle_penCurrentViewer (set) before dereferencing RT_sCurrentScene,
which is only set inside RT_AddParticlesForEntity and was null.

Fix: RT_GetViewVectors also requires RT_sCurrentScene, and
RT_Particle_RenderSquare/RenderLine/RenderQuad3D return early without a
scene; such particles were never flushed anyway (RT_Particle_Flush
already requires the scene), so the visible output is unchanged.
First-person chainsaw particles are not shown in RT (known limitation).

Same code in the TFE tree (file was identical; TFE has no chainsaw).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../Sources/Engine/Raytracing/RTParticles.cpp | 31 ++++++++++++++++---
 .../Sources/Engine/Raytracing/RTParticles.cpp | 31 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/SamTFE/Sources/Engine/Raytracing/RTParticles.cpp b/SamTFE/Sources/Engine/Raytracing/RTParticles.cpp
index 93e568bee4abab479c6bffa886c7883ecc8603e2..af0dbc978dfb5724fe661623d1ad9965e75228ff 100644
--- a/SamTFE/Sources/Engine/Raytracing/RTParticles.cpp
+++ b/SamTFE/Sources/Engine/Raytracing/RTParticles.cpp
@@ -236,7 +236,9 @@ static FLOAT3D RT_GetViewDirection()
 
 static void RT_GetViewVectors(FLOAT3D &x, FLOAT3D &y, ANGLE additionalBanking = 0)
 {
-  if (_Particle_penCurrentViewer != nullptr)
+  // SSTRE: the camera comes from the scene, so check the scene, not only the viewer
+  // (particles can be rendered outside of RT_AddParticlesForEntity, e.g. TSE chainsaw particles in the HUD pass)
+  if (_Particle_penCurrentViewer != nullptr && RT_sCurrentScene != nullptr)
   {
     const FLOATmatrix3D &m = RT_sCurrentScene->GetCameraRotation();
 
@@ -264,7 +266,14 @@ static void RT_GetViewVectors(FLOAT3D &x, FLOAT3D &y, ANGLE additionalBanking =
 
 
 void RT_Particle_RenderSquare(const FLOAT3D &vPos, FLOAT fSize, ANGLE aRotation, COLOR col, FLOAT fYRatio)
-{  
+{
+  // SSTRE: only particles of RT_AddParticlesForEntity can be submitted;
+  // others (e.g. first-person particles from a HUD pass) would never be flushed
+  if (RT_sCurrentScene == nullptr)
+  {
+    return;
+  }
+  
   // trivial rejection
   if (fSize < 0.0001f || ((col & CT_AMASK) >> CT_ASHIFT) < 2)
   {
@@ -309,7 +318,14 @@ void RT_Particle_RenderSquare(const FLOAT3D &vPos, FLOAT fSize, ANGLE aRotation,
 
 
 void RT_Particle_RenderLine(const FLOAT3D &a, const FLOAT3D &b, FLOAT width, COLOR col)
-{  
+{
+  // SSTRE: only particles of RT_AddParticlesForEntity can be submitted;
+  // others (e.g. first-person particles from a HUD pass) would never be flushed
+  if (RT_sCurrentScene == nullptr)
+  {
+    return;
+  }
+  
   // trivial rejection
   if (width < 0 || ((col & CT_AMASK) >> CT_ASHIFT) < 2)
   {
@@ -356,7 +372,14 @@ void RT_Particle_RenderLine(const FLOAT3D &a, const FLOAT3D &b, FLOAT width, COL
 
 
 void RT_Particle_RenderQuad3D(const FLOAT3D &vPos0, const FLOAT3D &vPos1, const FLOAT3D &vPos2, const FLOAT3D &vPos3, COLOR col)
-{ 
+{
+  // SSTRE: only particles of RT_AddParticlesForEntity can be submitted;
+  // others (e.g. first-person particles from a HUD pass) would never be flushed
+  if (RT_sCurrentScene == nullptr)
+  {
+    return;
+  }
+ 
   // trivial rejection
   if (((col & CT_AMASK) >> CT_ASHIFT) < 2)
   {
